__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
data/
# Public bearing datasets (CWRU etc.) are downloaded into data/, never
# committed: the CWRU Bearing Data Center publishes no licence, only
# "(c) Case Western Reserve University", so redistribution is not permitted.
# See ml/realdata/validate_public_dataset.py --help-download.
ml/artifacts/
*.db
# SQLite writes a sidecar journal next to the database; `*.db` does not match
# it, so `test_acoustic.db-journal` was committed. Found 2026-08-19 (F11).
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# macOS Finder metadata. Committed once, for the same reason: nothing was
# looking.
.DS_Store
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
# Vite writes a transient `vite.config.js.timestamp-<epoch>-<hash>.mjs` beside
# the config every time it loads it, and deletes it again — unless the process
# is killed first, which is what a test run or a Ctrl-C does. Seven of them had
# already been committed by 2026-08-20, one per interrupted dev session, all
# regenerable and none meaningful. Third instance of the same miss after
# `.DS_Store` and `test_acoustic.db-journal`: tool scratch files accumulate
# faster than anyone notices, because no test ever looks at the file list.
frontend/vite.config.js.timestamp-*
.env
.venv/
output/
pytest-cache-files-*/
firmware/baseline.npz
# The v2 brief arrived in a folder literally named "use this now " WITH a
# trailing space. Git strips trailing whitespace from .gitignore patterns
# unless it is backslash-escaped, so the rule below never matched and the
# folder was committed anyway (F11). The brief itself is worth keeping and now
# lives in the v2 spec (not in this public copy)/; the two .py files in there were byte-identical
# copies of ml/simulate.py and ml/verify_signals.py, which is exactly the
# duplicate-source trap that caused the two-repository divergence. Pattern
# widened so a stray trailing space can never sneak past again.
use this now*/
